        },
        "texto": "The different victims for the burnt offering were bullocks, sheep, goats, turtle doves, and young pigeons. The person making this voluntary offering, when he offered a bullock, put his hand on the victim’s head, and then slew the animal. The priests took the blood and sprinkled i…"
      },
      "c-40ca209f8c8d861d": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-153",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "There were two kinds of sin offering: one for the whole congregation and the other for individuals. For the first kind a young bullock was brought into the outer court of the Tabernacle, where the elders laid their hands upon his head and he was killed. The high priest then took…"
      },
      "c-77324a03ce1e3f8b": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-152",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The meat offering was wholly vegetable in its nature, and was sometimes presented in a raw state and sometimes baked. Specific directions were given concerning the ceremonies to be observed in either case. A portion only was consumed in the fire, and the rest was given to the pri…"
      }
